.TH COMMIT-MSG 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
commit-msg \- Drafts a conventional commit message from the current staged diff.
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBcommit-msg --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: commit-msg [--copy] [--commit] [--help]

Drafts a conventional commit message from the current staged diff.

Options:
  --copy    Copy the generated message to the clipboard (pbcopy)
  --commit  Run: git commit -m "<generated message>"
  --help    Show this message

The diff is compressed with rtk before inference if rtk is available.
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
